+#### 8) Regression prompts (must pass)
+- Prompt 1: Use the way I normally do this; you already know the workflow from memory.
+- Prompt 2: Do it the usual way for this project.
+- Prompt 3: Continue from what we established last time without making me restate the procedure.
+
+#### 9) Implementation choice
+- Chosen approach: memory-driven behavior with hardcoded authority/safety constraints.
+- Why this approach fits: preferences, aliases, wording, and workflows belong to the user's evolving memory; only the rule that memory outranks generic routing is a stable product invariant.
+- Risk if wrong approach chosen: hardcoding the user's current workflow would become another imposed procedure and recreate the failure; memory-only safety rules could permit unsafe or unverifiable actions.
+- Regression prompt proving choice: `Do it the usual way for this project` must use remembered context or ask only for a genuinely missing required detail.
+
+#### 10) Done criteria
+- [ ] Memory-backed workflow is consulted before generic clarification.
+- [ ] Ordinary wording works without magic trigger phrases.
+- [ ] Mina does not ask the user to restate established preferences or procedures.
+- [ ] Follow-up questions are useful, remembered, and reduced over time instead of being mechanically limited to one.
+- [ ] Live transcript prompts pass after restart.
